# Payment Transaction Webhook Configuration
# Canonical production path: deploy/.env.production
# Local development path: .env
# Note: Container image digests live separately in deploy/.release.env.
# Build toolchain: Go 1.27.2 (go.mod, Docker builders and CI); rebuild images
# for stdlib CVE-2026-78667 / CVE-2026-97031 fixes; retain the Trivy security gate.

# Application Environment (production | development)
APP_ENV=production

# Runtime role: "gateway" for HTTP gateway slots, "worker" for payment/outbox singleton, or "monolith-dev" for local development only.
# Production strictly rejects "monolith-dev" and requires explicit role assignment on each service container.
RUNTIME_ROLE=

LISTEN_ADDR=0.0.0.0:8080
PORT=8090
# Public domain of the dashboard used for Origin, CSRF validation, and dynamic Traefik route derivation
PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://bank.tuannguyenviet.site
# Public domain of the anonymous transaction viewer (no Cloudflare Access)
PUBLIC_VIEWER_HOST=transactions.tuannguyenviet.site
# Optional explicit route acknowledgement URL traversing edge ingress (defaults to http://127.0.0.1:80/readyz)
# ROUTE_ACK_URL=http://127.0.0.1:80/readyz
DATA_DIR=/data
DATABASE_PATH=/data/gateway.db
TZ=Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh

# payOS-only payments using KienlongBank. All three credentials must come from
# the same dedicated collection channel; do not share its webhook with another app.
# Required in production even when new payments are disabled. Secret files are
# readonly mounts; never commit their contents. Direct PAYOS_CLIENT_ID,
# PAYOS_API_KEY, and PAYOS_CHECKSUM_KEY are also supported for local development.
PAYOS_CLIENT_ID_FILE=/run/secrets/payos_client_id
PAYOS_API_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/payos_api_key
PAYOS_CHECKSUM_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/payos_checksum_key
# Exact origin only: HTTPS, no trailing slash/path/query/userinfo/fragment.
# Development may use http://localhost:5173 or a loopback IP HTTP origin.
# Fixed QR URL: <origin>/pay; webhook: <origin>/api/integrations/payos/webhook.
PAYMENT_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://transactions.tuannguyenviet.site
# Safe rollout example: keep new orders disabled until webhook confirmation and
# live acceptance. Defaults are true / false; neither flag enables an ACB fallback.
# Issued-order callbacks/reconciliation remain active while new orders are disabled.
# Stored order snapshots, admin lists and reviews do not require a live provider.
# Unconfigured development can inspect saved data; create/cancel/confirm stay unavailable.
PAYMENTS_ENABLED=false
PAYOS_WEBHOOK_CONFIRMED=false
# Application limit, not a claim about the provider's maximum. Integer VND.
PAYMENT_MAX_AMOUNT_VND=500000000
# Payment intents persist before provider requests: retry the same UUID
# Idempotency-Key after a timeout; never automatically replace it with a new key.
# Orders expire after 30 minutes. Migration 14 preserves ACB history and pending
# notification deliveries; do not restore a pre-payOS DB after issuing an order.
# Verified callbacks and signed provider reconciliation share one atomic receipt,
# transaction, event journal and notification-outbox commit. Callback replays do
# not create another credit. Unknown/mismatched verified callbacks remain in the
# private review inbox; missing-binding callbacks are consumed after signed Get.
# Public payment APIs are same-origin JSON, no-store, and identify each order by
# a random capability. Public SSE/history expose orderCode correlation only,
# never the capability, checkout link, VA or channel credentials.
# QR URL /pay is camera-scanned, not a reusable bank-app static VietQR. Guest
# amounts are VND; cashier inputs are positive integer thousands of VND.
# The cashier retains up to three durable order capabilities across reloads.
# Removing a card does not cancel its order. Guest /pay pages never play shop TTS.
# Worker owns payment reconciliation and the durable notification dispatcher;
# gateways never schedule bank/provider polling. Quiesce drains active payment
# requests before deliveries and retains the durable journal watermark.
# One-time dbtool -payos-cutover -lease-token requires a valid locked deployment
# lease after legacy writers stop; it preserves history and audits PAYOS_CUTOVER.
# Legacy auth-count/session-check CLI actions and ACB login/poll routes are removed.
# Production migration 14 (poll rows matched) stays immutable; payOS orders
# use migration 15. Cutover snapshots pin actual legacy schema 13 or 14.
# First cutover: stage deploy.yml target=all, deploy=false, rehearse=false;
# pin successful source SHA/run, image digests and bundle checksums. Do not run
# normal deploy against legacy manifests (PAYOS_RUNTIME_MIGRATION_REQUIRED).
# DEPLOY_PATH=/opt/bank-event-gateway bash migrate-payos-runtime.sh --check <SHA>
# reads prerequisites only. BOTH --check and --apply <SHA> require
# --source-run-id and --prior-frontend JSON
# {app,sha,version_id,central_run_id,bank_access_headers_file}. Keep the Access
# header file private. All five pinned candidate images must be prefetched;
# explicit SQLite volume read/write deployment permission is required (root or
# DB owner, not broad auto-sudo). Read --help for resumable evidence inputs.
# Root/operator must install reviewed canonical blue/green route policies with
# install-route-publisher.sh --upgrade <absolute-template-dir> before --apply.
# Callback ingress is exact POST, 64 KiB, 60 requests/second (burst 120); capability
# API routers disable access logs and send no-store/no-referrer headers.
# Confirm requires owner evidence while creates stay disabled. Enable creates
# only for user-paid live acceptance; receipts/journal/deliveries must prove it.
# --rollback-before-payments cannot restore legacy DB after any issued order or
# receipt (PAYOS_ROLLBACK_REQUIRES_PAYMENT_DRAIN). Keep current DB/receiver and
# reconcile issued orders when rolling back a payOS-compatible frontend/runtime.
# Normal deploy rejects a pending migration. Before LIVE, a different candidate
# needs a separately reviewed forward-repair plan; pinned --apply can resume.
# dbtool -payment-counts is readonly and never auto-migrates schema.


# Encryption key for notification secrets and retained encrypted historical data.
# In production, APP_MASTER_KEY_FILE is mandatory and direct APP_MASTER_KEY is rejected.
# Generate via: openssl rand -hex 32 > /run/secrets/app_master_key
APP_MASTER_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/app_master_key

# Backup Configuration (age Encryption)
# Asymmetric public recipient for encrypting backups at rest.
# Private identity key is stored off-host and NEVER placed on the VPS.
BACKUP_AGE_RECIPIENT=age1...
BACKUP_DIR=/var/backups/acb
# Optional hook executed after backup publish (receives artifact path and manifest path)
OFFHOST_BACKUP_HOOK=/usr/local/bin/acb-offhost-backup
REQUIRE_OFFHOST_BACKUP=0

# Cloudflare Access (Zero Trust) Authentication (Required for Production Dashboard)
# The backend validates JWT issuer, audience, expiry, nbf, and JWKS signatures.
CLOUDFLARE_ACCESS_TEAM_NAME=your-team
CLOUDFLARE_ACCESS_AUD=replace-with-access-application-audience
CF_ACCESS_ISSUER=https://your-team.cloudflareaccess.com
CF_ACCESS_AUDIENCE=replace-with-access-application-audience
CF_ACCESS_JWKS_URL=https://your-team.cloudflareaccess.com/cdn-cgi/access/certs

# Comma-separated Cloudflare JWT identity subjects (e.g. operator emails)
OWNER_SUBJECTS=admin@example.com
OPERATOR_SUBJECTS=
VIEWER_SUBJECTS=

WORKER_RPC_URL=http://worker:8190
WORKER_INTERNAL_TOKEN_FILE=/run/secrets/worker_internal_token

# Runtime secret paths only; host secrets directory: 0700, files: 0600,
# owner 1000:1000. APP_MASTER_KEY_FILE is defined above.
